# stdout:
Replace this knapsack binary with the newest release's, after checking the
download's SHA-256.

A knapsack built with go install, or installed by a package manager, is
updated the same way it was installed; self-update says how.

Every command checks for a newer release once a day, and version every
time, and says so on stderr. Set KNAPSACK_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER to stop that.

Usage:
  knapsack self-update [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for self-update

Global Flags:
      --config string   use this config file instead of the default
  -v, --verbose         show progress and the underlying cause of errors
# stderr:
